 "realtime_factor": 0.017039358825704475,
 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Tents can be set up pretty quickly, and the tent light helps a lot. If you can stay in for an hour or two after the tent is up, the dark gets easier. Cook the sticks off the bone and keep the sauce. The sticks taste just as good as they look, and the sauce keeps well. The sauce can be frozen. Freeze it in a bottle that can be frozen, so you can pull it out straight without having to reheat the whole thing. Let them keep the sticks and have the sauce. A decent rice pudding is easy and tastes like home. Then make it the next day when you' back in the tent. It gets easier with practice, and the sticks keep well in an airtight box.",
